Source: faceunlock
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: faceunlock maintainers <faceunlock@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), libpam0g-dev, gcc
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://localhost/faceunlock

Package: faceunlock
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.10),
         python3-numpy,
         libc6,
         libgcc-s1,
         libstdc++6,
         zlib1g,
         libpam0g,
         libpam-runtime,
         pkexec | policykit-1
Description: face recognition login for Linux (PAM module + management CLI)
 faceunlock uses YuNet (detection) and SFace (128-d embedding) on a plain RGB
 webcam, and wires the result into PAM so that it covers the GDM login screen,
 the GNOME lock screen, sudo, su and pkexec/polkit prompts.
 .
 人脸识别登录（PAM 模块 + 命令行管理工具）。
 .
 Security stance: this is a CONVENIENCE factor, not a replacement for your
 password. Any failure - no face, no camera, camera busy, timeout, remote
 session, tampered template, unexpected exception - falls back to the password
 prompt and never locks you out. A plain RGB camera cannot defeat a photo or
 screen replay attack, so do not rely on it alone for high-value targets.
 .
 安全定位：便捷因子。任何失败都会回退密码，绝不锁死系统；纯 RGB 摄像头
 无法防照片翻拍。
 .
 Ubuntu 26.04 (polkit 127) runs the pkexec authentication helper inside a
 hardened systemd sandbox (PrivateDevices=yes, DevicePolicy=strict), which hides
 /dev/video* from the PAM stack. This package therefore ships a systemd drop-in
 that re-allows *video devices only* for polkit-agent-helper@.service, so face
 authentication also works in graphical authorization dialogs. Disable it with
 `faceunlock polkit-camera off`; the login screen, lock screen, sudo and su are
 unaffected, only pkexec falls back to the password.
 .
 授权框（pkexec）的人脸能力靠一个 systemd drop-in 放开 polkit helper 的**视频设备**
 权限换取（Ubuntu 26.04 / polkit 127 的沙箱会隐藏 /dev/video*）。不想接受这个取舍
 可执行 `sudo faceunlock polkit-camera off`，其它场景不受影响。

Package: faceunlock-gui
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         faceunlock (= ${binary:Version})
Description: graphical manager for faceunlock (Tauri + WebKitGTK)
 人脸识别管理界面。
 .
 提供：人脸的新增 / 重命名 / 删除；摄像头实时预览与检测框；识别测试
 （可视化相似度分数与阈值参考线）；阈值与场景开关（登录+锁屏 / sudo /
 su / pkexec）；一键停用（panic）。
 .
 特权操作通过 pkexec 调用 org.faceunlock.manage 这个 polkit 动作，
 界面本身以普通用户身份运行，不持有 root 权限。

Package: faceunlock-full
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.10),
         python3-numpy,
         libc6,
         libgcc-s1,
         libstdc++6,
         zlib1g,
         libpam0g,
         libpam-runtime,
         pkexec | policykit-1
Conflicts: faceunlock, faceunlock-gui
Replaces: faceunlock, faceunlock-gui
Provides: faceunlock (= ${binary:Version}), faceunlock-gui (= ${binary:Version})
Description: face recognition login for Linux - complete bundle (核心 + 图形界面)
 自包含完整包：一个 .deb 装完全部内容，不需要再单独装 faceunlock 与
 faceunlock-gui。
 .
 包含：PAM 模块 pam_faceunlock.so、root 认证助手、命令行工具、
 YuNet+SFace ONNX 模型、随包分发的 OpenCV 4.11、Tauri 图形管理界面、
 polkit 授权动作、pam-configs 配置档与 man page。
 .
 与拆分包的关系：本包 Conflicts/Replaces/Provides faceunlock 与
 faceunlock-gui，因此**同一时刻只能装其中一套**。从拆分包切到本包时，
 安装脚本会自动记住"原本人脸是否为启用状态"并在切换后恢复
 （标记放在 /run 里，重启即失效，不会留下陈旧状态）。
 .
 安全定位与拆分包一致：便捷因子，任何失败都回退密码，绝不锁死系统；
 纯 RGB 摄像头无法防照片翻拍。
 .
 Ubuntu 26.04 (polkit 127) sandboxes the pkexec authentication helper
 (PrivateDevices=yes), hiding /dev/video* from the PAM stack, and its stderr is
 part of the polkit<->agent protocol stream. This version therefore (a) skips
 face auth in milliseconds when no video device is visible, (b) never writes to
 a non-tty stderr from the PAM helper, and (c) ships a systemd drop-in that
 re-allows *video devices only* for polkit-agent-helper@.service, so face
 authentication also works in graphical authorization dialogs. Disable that with
 `faceunlock polkit-camera off`; only pkexec falls back to the password.
 .
 授权框（pkexec）的人脸能力靠一个 systemd drop-in 放开 polkit helper 的**视频设备**
 权限换取；沙箱里没有摄像头时会毫秒级回退密码（不再卡住授权框）。
 不想要该例外可执行 `sudo faceunlock polkit-camera off`。
